infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title Where the optimizer runs — three cost surfaces, one srcset
  desc Same next/image markup; the optimizer's bill changes shape with where it transforms
  lists
    - label Vercel — metered per source image
      desc Each plan bundles a transformation quota; a 40,000-SKU catalog blows through the included thousands fast, and every new source image after that is billable.
    - label Self-hosted — CPU plus persistent disk
      desc sharp spends ~100–300 ms re-encoding each variant; the cache lives in .next/cache/images and must survive deploys, or the whole catalog re-encodes every release as a daily CPU sawtooth.
    - label Custom loader — a dedicated image CDN
      desc Rewrite URLs to Cloudinary, imgix, or Thumbor — keep the next/image markup benefits (srcset, dimensions, lazy/priority) while moving transformation onto infrastructure built for it.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b
